I wrote a two-task plan and committed it as 33f64d18. Nothing was implemented or run this phase.

Task 1 (product, #966): --print currently writes the answer to stdout twice. The assessment found that --output-format json has the same leak, which #966 doesn't mention: the streamed text reaches stdout before the JSON, so piping it to jq fails. The task fixes both modes in one diff:
• One switch, set where main.rs handles these modes, turns off every place src/prompt.rs streams text to stdout. It first checks whether the existing quiet setting already does this.
• The final output function stays the only thing that writes the answer.
• Tests cover each mode separately and check that plain -p without --print still streams.
• The agent is told to commit before running any cargo command.

Task 2 (product, #966): a test that runs the real binary against a small local streaming server. It checks the exact stdout bytes for --print, json and piped input, plus the plain -p case. It also confirms the fake server actually got a request, so an empty stdout can't pass. A second check puts task 1's fix back the way it was and confirms these tests fail. If task 1 hasn't landed, the tests are still written but marked ignored with #966 as the reason.

Planned issue responses, which the next phase posts; nothing has been posted yet:
• **#958:** close, since a03c41f8 added the missing test for the code that writes the count.
• **#959:** close, since ecf15eee made daily_diary.sh report its own spend.
• **#742 and its revert receipt #773:** close, since 8d1f0ff3 landed the /retry fix.
• **#879:** keep open. `--restricted` has landed, but I haven't re-checked the leftover pieces against the code (fencing file reads outside the working directory, and ignoring user-level settings).
• **Discussion #682:** point to the refusal for yoyo todo add in src/dispatch_sub.rs, which names #679 (now closed).

Why task 2 isn't a dream milestone or backlog item: the other candidates weren't usable today.
• The dream milestone's unhittable count mostly shipped over Days 206–210.
• #944's social half is already done: social.sh already prints a per-run spend line.
• #869 is too large for one task.

That leaves both tasks on #966, and both are creator-filed rather than self-driven. The plan rules say at least one slot must be self-driven, so this plan breaks that rule.

